WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.306
Hi, I'm Marshal.

00:00:02.306 --> 00:00:07.050
A mixture of experts keeps many feed-forward networks and runs a few per token.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:07.727
Who decides?

00:00:10.433 --> 00:00:14.843
Qwen3 has a hundred and twenty-eight experts in each of its forty-eight layers.

00:00:15.263 --> 00:00:17.677
For each token, a router picks eight of them.

00:00:17.677 --> 00:00:19.554
The rest sit idle for that token.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.093
The router scores every expert with one matrix and a softmax.

00:00:25.513 --> 00:00:26.890
It keeps the eight highest.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:29.093
Every other expert gets a weight of zero.

00:00:29.513 --> 00:00:32.144
The eight weights are rescaled so they add up to one.

00:00:33.913 --> 00:00:37.563
The token's output is those eight experts' outputs, weighted and summed.

00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:43.584
GShard put this layer inside the Transformer, in every other block, with

00:00:43.584 --> 00:00:44.906
two experts per token.

00:00:45.286 --> 00:00:49.196
Spread over devices, each token travels to its experts and back.

00:00:49.196 --> 00:00:50.973
Two exchanges in every layer.

00:00:52.408 --> 00:00:56.869
Hardware wants fixed shapes, so each expert gets a fixed number of slots.

00:00:56.869 --> 00:00:57.898
Busy experts overflow.

00:00:58.318 --> 00:01:01.631
Overflow tokens are dropped and ride the residual connection.

00:01:01.631 --> 00:01:04.943
More slots drop fewer, and empty slots still cost.

00:01:05.363 --> 00:01:07.261
Even routing fits a small buffer.

00:01:07.261 --> 00:01:10.423
That is why every mixture of experts fights for balance.

00:01:12.408 --> 00:01:16.224
Balance used to come from an extra loss that fights the main one.

00:01:16.224 --> 00:01:19.159
DeepSeek replaced it with a bias, used only to choose.

00:01:19.539 --> 00:01:23.162
Overloaded experts get their bias lowered, idle ones raised.

00:01:23.162 --> 00:01:24.369
No gradient touched.

00:01:25.658 --> 00:01:27.965
Where the balance is measured matters.

00:01:27.965 --> 00:01:30.656
Balanced per sequence, every domain spreads evenly.

00:01:31.036 --> 00:01:33.460
Balanced over a whole batch, experts specialise.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.885
Code and maths find their own experts.

00:01:37.492 --> 00:01:39.707
So I read a real router.

00:01:39.707 --> 00:01:44.137
Qwen3 on my 3090, every expert choice in all forty-eight layers, over

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:46.353
code, prose, word problems and LaTeX.

00:01:46.733 --> 00:01:49.723
Pooled over all four, the load is a smooth slope.

00:01:49.723 --> 00:01:51.218
Almost every expert gets used.

00:01:51.598 --> 00:01:53.834
Split by domain, it breaks apart.

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:56.442
Each domain leaves hundreds of experts untouched.

00:01:57.592 --> 00:02:01.502
In an average layer, prose never reaches about seventeen of the

00:02:01.502 --> 00:02:02.924
hundred and twenty-eight experts.

00:02:02.924 --> 00:02:06.478
Code and prose share almost none of their busiest experts.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.841
A batch reads the union of what its tokens chose.

00:02:11.841 --> 00:02:15.989
Eight users touch nearly forty-seven experts a layer, close to a random guess.

00:02:16.409 --> 00:02:20.605
Consecutive tokens from one sequence share experts, so sixty-four of them read

00:02:20.605 --> 00:02:22.004
only half the layer.

00:02:23.425 --> 00:02:27.716
Put that routing through a Switch-style buffer and a single sequence's batch

00:02:27.716 --> 00:02:29.504
loses half its expert work.

00:02:29.504 --> 00:02:32.007
Specialised models run without a fixed buffer.

00:02:33.225 --> 00:02:36.037
Balance over the whole corpus, and experts specialise.

00:02:36.037 --> 00:02:39.551
That is the trade every modern mixture of experts makes.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:45.281
A router that picks a few, a buffer that drops the overflow,

00:02:45.281 --> 00:02:47.097
and experts that learn their domain.

00:02:47.097 --> 00:02:48.005
Thanks for watching!

00:02:48.425 --> 00:02:50.577
Every source is in the full article.

00:02:50.577 --> 00:02:51.192
I'm Marshal.

00:02:51.192 --> 00:02:51.500
Bye!
